blackbeard akainu shanks who will be the  final boss of one piece oda sensei has  treated us to some perfectly punishable  builds throughout one piece but as we  near the final saga we can probably  count the major enemies that luffy will  beat down on one hand so today we'll  explore who we most want to see luffy go  toe to toe with as we wonder will we  ever get a punch as satisfying as the  one where he knocked the color right out  of san charlos the two foes at the top  of everyone's list are of course a kainu  and blackbeard what makes them the  perfect final opponent for luffy is that  both blackbeard and akainu are the  perfect representatives of their  factions in the one piece world oh also  quickly massive shout out to blackbird  and skyberry my two subscribers of the  day thanks for hitting subscribe for new  content and helping me raise my bouncy  let's start with akainu cause he is the  quintessential marine as the fleet  admiral he represents everything that  this organization stands for and he is  the de facto leader ignoring as he  sometimes does the gorosei he is a  believer in absolute justice in  zakazuki's eyes no crime should go  unpunished all pirates automatically are  criminals and he is the appointed judge  jury and executioner as much as enes  lobby would like to have a say in that  even if he fundamentally disagrees with  the gorosei or the celestial dragons he  will do everything in his power to  uphold the order that the world  government represents according to him a  world must be founded on strict rules  and authority without submitting to this  ordered hierarchy the world will descend  into anarchy and chaos a chaos that the  world of piracy embodies for him and to  him this doesn't extend only to pirates  that inflict actual violence upon  innocent people like the donkey hot  pirates even the carefree adventuring  that the straw hat crew engages in risks  corroding the balance of society and so  this of course makes him the perfect  counter to luffy who believes that  everyone should be free to choose their  own destinies and follow their dreams to  party to eat to the fill and to  adventure akainu would of course stomp  all these things out in service of  making a more tightly structured world  our first introduction to akaino shows  us just how far he's willing to go in  the name of absolute justice on the  island of o'hara he single-handedly  killed a ship full of innocent citizens  fleeing the buster call none of the  people there were even the librarians  who held the secrets of the ponyglyphs  in fact these evacuees left robin to die  on the island so they could themselves  escape however akainu felt that even the  smallest chance that someone leaving the  island held the librarian secrets posed  too great a risk to the world government  and so to the horror of even another  admiral like aokiji he just destroyed  the ship along with everyone on it  blackbeard on the other hand is of  course the perfect representative of the  world of piracy like luffy he is one of  the yonko the four emperors of the new  world and a prime candidate in the race  to find the one piece if you were to ask  a random person on the street to name  one pirate a real live one chances are  pretty high they'd say blackbeard likely  they might not even know the name of any  other real real-life pirates honestly  they'd soon have come up with captain  jack sparrow before they actually got to  end bonnie or francis drake's oda sensei  gave marshall the teach the title of  blackbeard because he embodies the  classic image of a pirate at least he  represents a certain type of pirates in  the original romans dawn one shots  before the serialization of one piece as  we know it oda sensei actually defined  two separate classifications of pirates  pirates that are looking for adventure  on the high seas like the straw hats  were termed peas main pirates whereas  pirates who pillage and plunder were  called morganeers by oda and so while  oda sensei didn't keep the terminology  we can still see echoes of this  definition in the different approaches  to piracy that different crews take and  the blackbeard pirates are definitely in  the morgan ear plundering type of camp  now you might think that we haven't  really seen him do much in the way of  classic pillaging and plundering but the  very first reference we get to black bit  in the series actually confirms this  back on drum island dalton refers to  blackbeard ransacking the kingdom in  fact it was the terrifying power of the  blackbeard pirates that caused wapol to  flee the country and take all the  doctors with him setting us up for  chopper's introduction and let's just  take another minute to once again praise  the almighty godas foreshadowing because  we received whispers of blackbeard long  before luffy and blackbeard's chance  encounter on jaya by now making their  home on beehive island the blackbeard  pirates are creating their version of a  pirate paradise lawless and chaotic he  allows his 10 titanic captains to run  wild in a new world as they amass power  by collecting more and more devil fruits  so how are both of these characters the  perfect final enemies for luffy while at  their core both of these antagonists are  complete opposites to luffy's core  philosophy luffy believes in freedom  above all else freedom to travel to eat  to party to adventure and yeah freedom  to live a kaino and the marines restrict  the freedom of people across the seas of  one piece while they may protect the  people from dangerous violent pirates  they also enact exploitative taxes  restrict travel and even run protection  for the slave-holding celestial dragons  blackbeard on the other hand instead of  being opposed to luffy is more like the  other side of the same coin just like  luffy teach believes in a kind of  freedom but it's a freedom that allows  someone to use their power to infringe  on the freedom of another in other words  kind of a rule of the strongest if he  wants so while luffy uses his freedom to  uplift others and grant them the same  freedoms he has blackbeard uses his  freedom towards his own personal gains  and pushing others down and it's not  just that their philosophies are  diametrically opposed that set a kind  and blackbeard up as the perfect  antagonist for luffy the stakes here are  personal as well these two characters  are both directly responsible for aces  death a kainu very literally did kill  ace and to add to luffy's personal  grudge against the fleet admiral he  killed aes while ace was trying to  protect luffy however the war at marine  ford never would have occurred in the  first place if it weren't for the  actions of blackbeard he was the one who  captured ace and turned him over to the  marines in order to claim his status as  a shichibukai this too partly falls onto  luffy's shoulders because blackbeard was  actually pursuing luffy at the time that  ace confronted him and so before the end  of the series i think we can all agree  that we do need to see luffy take his  revenge on these powerful foes another  figure that will probably see luffy  fight before the end of one piece is the  mysterious insama so far really almost  nothing is known about the secret true  ruler of the world government given that  they've only appeared in a single  chapter of the manga there is still a  lot that we have to learn about this  shadowy figure but given that they're  the head of the world government they  appear to be very much final boss  material yes luffy does have a personal  grudge against the kainu but eem is a  kaino's boss's boss and the real  decision maker behind all the actions of  the marines so if luffy actually wants  to bring freedom to the rest of the  world the only way he will be able to do  that is go through and we also know that  im sama has it out for luffy as well i  mean yes we don't really know too much  about eem's true motivations but  whenever i rip up a picture of someone's  face it usually means i don't really  like them we also have a few wild cards  though these are figures that luffy  could possibly fight but we really don't  know yet at this point whether they're  enemy or friends a big one that people  of course have been theorizing about  including me is the possibility that  luffy will fight his childhood hero  shanks based on shanks's weird  connection to the gorosei some fans have  speculated that shanks's motivation  might be less than good perhaps he will  actually turn out to be a true rival or  even the main villain to luffy for the  throne of pirate king i actually just  released a video about just this  possibility because i truly believe that  one way or another shanks and luffy will  clash at some point very soon in the  story who knows maybe they'll just have  a good spirited davy backfight leading  to the 12th and final straw hats lucky  room or it might be an all-out battle  then of course we have absolutely wild  predictions as we know oda sensei is  famous for his ridiculous left turns and  unpredictability  so who else could luffy still have to  fight i mean the sky is the limit really  perhaps he'll have a rematch against one  of the series first villains and fellow  yonko buggy the clown after all at the  rate that buggy is failing upwards at  the moment he might be a true rival for  the position of pirate king at this  point maybe he'll also be forced into a  conflict with a marine that he has close  ties to since he is after all still a  pirate we've built up a metric ton of  hatred for a kainu but wouldn't it be  heartbreaking to see him have to go all  out against kobe or smoka or even his  grandfather garp after all people have  really been sleeping on kobe future  admiral the secret final villain that  oda has foreshadowed since chapter two  his future power only makes sense given  that he is a child of big mom as  evidenced by his pink hair  okay maybe i might have to lay off the  coffee i might be hitting those theories  a little bit too hard and i wasn't being  quite serious but the fight i'm probably  looking forward to the most is in fact  shanks and if you want to understand why  this clash between luffy and shanks is  inevitable you should really not miss  out on this video right here
 

